WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.238
This is the store table, and
both parts point back to it.

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:07.437
There are eight places an attribute can
live, in the order to reach for them.

3
00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:09.113
Native properties first.

4
00:00:09.113 --> 00:00:14.725
Then extension attributes one to fifteen,
which rules can read but anyone can see.

5
00:00:14.725 --> 00:00:17.488
Directory extensions when
you need more slots.

6
00:00:17.488 --> 00:00:22.288
Custom security attributes for sensitive
values that dynamic rules can't read.

7
00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:28.301
Then device properties, Azure tags, and
certificate user I Ds, the PIV binding.

8
00:00:28.301 --> 00:00:30.338
Pick the store by who has to read it.

9
00:00:30.338 --> 00:00:31.560
Now, the path.
